-Face Contouring (also called `ContourFaceProc`) is a recursive procedure that processes the faces of an octree to generate triangle indices during the mesh generation phase of Manifold Dual Contouring [S1, unofficial]. It operates on pairs of octree nodes, recursing into children for internal nodes and invoking the sibling Edge Contouring method for leaf nodes [S1, unofficial].
+Face Contouring (`ContourFaceProc`) is a recursive procedure that processes octree faces to generate triangle indices during the mesh generation phase of Manifold Dual Contouring [S1, unofficial]. It traverses internal nodes to resolve child faces and delegates edge resolution to the sibling Edge Contouring method, ensuring manifold connectivity across varying octree levels [S1, unofficial].
 
